# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads.
#
# Without this file gcloud derives its exclusions from `.gitignore`, and it reads
# only the top-level one. `frontend/node_modules` is ignored by
# `frontend/.gitignore`, which gcloud never looks at, so the first upload was
# 10,065 files and 121 MiB of Linux-incompatible native modules that the build
# then discarded and rebuilt with `npm ci`.
#
# This is the upload, not the image. `.dockerignore` governs what the daemon sees
# once the tarball is unpacked, and anything excluded here never reaches either -
# so every path the Dockerfile copies has to survive this list.
#
# EVERY PATTERN IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and that is not style. This file
# uses .gitignore syntax, where a bare name matches at any depth - unlike
# .dockerignore, whose patterns are relative to the context root. The first
# version of this file was written as if the two were the same, and cost two
# failed builds:
#
#   `supabase`  also matched `app/infrastructure/supabase/`, so the image shipped
#               without its database client and uvicorn died on
#               ModuleNotFoundError before binding a port;
#   `*.md`      would have matched every file in `prompts/`, which is where the
#               agent prompts live - a subtler failure, since the container would
#               have started and then failed on the first agent call.

/.git
/.gitignore

# Rebuilt inside the image, and the wrong platform's binaries besides.
/.venv
/frontend/node_modules
/frontend/dist

# Never. Secrets reach the service through Secret Manager, and the build gets what
# it needs through --substitutions.
/.env
/.env.*
!/.env.example
/frontend/.env
/frontend/.env.*

# Depth-matched on purpose: bytecode is worth excluding wherever it is.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

/.mypy_cache
/.pytest_cache
/.ruff_cache
/.coverage
/coverage.xml
/htmlcov

# Not build inputs: the suite, the schema history, the specification. Note
# `/supabase` is the top-level migrations directory, NOT
# `app/infrastructure/supabase`, which the application imports.
/tests
/migrations
/supabase
/PlantCare_AI_Spec
/docs
/scripts/*.py

# Root-level prose only. `prompts/` is full of .md files and they are runtime
# inputs, not documentation.
/*.md
